    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-ceiling output of **Kyle Tucker** (74.70) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.51). **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a favorable matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez, whose 4.53 xERA provides the right environment for power extraction, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a dynamic platoon advantage that more than compensates for a minor BvP hurdle. **Andy Pages** also projects as a high-value play (69.40) in the same contest against Rodriguez; his ability to drive the ball in that matchup makes him a core component of today's offensive strategy. While **Nasim Nunez** (57.11) occupies the bottom of the lineup, his inclusion is tactical: the slow delivery of Sandy Alcantara creates a high-leverage opportunity for him to exploit the basepaths, a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the scarcest category, SB.\n\nThe decision-making process for the utility and infield slots remained tight, particularly for **Josh Jung** (54.71) and **Liam Hicks** (51.05). Both players cleared the \"marginal\" threshold comfortably, but their upside is somewhat muted by opposing pitchers like McGreevy and Cavalli who maintain decent xERA metrics. **Miguel Vargas** (42.56) remains our lowest-scored starter, barely edging out internal depth options; he faces a tough assignment against Ryan, whose 3.21 xERA presents the most significant hurdle for our offense today. While we are currently carrying injured assets like **Luis Robert Jr.** and navigating off-days for key contributors like **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill**, the roster remains optimized to maximize daily efficiency. We are closely monitoring the lineup status of **Liam Hicks**; if his \"Lineup Pending\" status shifts downward or results in a benching, we have contingency plans involving **Drake Baldwin** or **Jacob Wilson** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 landscape.",
